  "lineage": "Yaqui (Yoeme) pascola-and-matachín Easter Week ceremonial dance-cycle of the Yaqui communities of Sonora (Mexico) and southern Arizona, integrating pre-contact Yaqui ceremonial structure with sixteenth-century Spanish-Jesuit liturgical introductions into a syncretic Yaqui-Catholic Easter cycle. The pascola \"old men of the fiesta\" dancers wear carved-wood masks and dance to harp-and-violin music in the village dance-ramada throughout the multi-day ceremonial cycle; the matachín soldiers-of-the-Virgin dance-society performs in colorful crown-and-staff regalia. Performance: continuous days-long ceremonial-cycle with multiple specialized music-and-dance functions including the canónigos solemn liturgical procession, the venado-deer-dance hunting ceremony, and the matachín-soldier-of-the-Virgin processional.",
